  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Maryland recorded $706M in contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Obligations fell 98.2% year over year. Maryland had 2,903 awards with an average award size of $243K. Year-to-date buying concentrated in a few agencies: the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $246M, and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $182M. Top vendors include THE JOHNS HOPKINS UNIVERSITY APPLIED PHYSICS LABORATORY LLC at $132M and C&T TECHNOLOGIES LLC at $38.6M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences is the largest industry with $157M, followed by Other Computer Related Services at $134M. Recent fiscal-year history shows big swings: FY22 obligations were $43B, FY23 were $42.6B, FY24 were $47.4B, FY25 were $40.7B, and FY26 were $38.4B. FY27 obligations so far stand at $706M. These figures are contract obligations and reflect fiscal year to date activity only.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are buying in Maryland right now?",
        "body": "The Department of Health and Human Services is the largest buyer, obligating $246M in FY2027 to date. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration follows with $182M. The Department of Homeland Security and the Department of Veterans Affairs are also significant buyers, obligating $85.1M and $68.6M respectively. Several civilian agencies including the General Services Administration and the Department of Transportation contributed $58.7M and $30.3M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors and industries are receiving Maryland contract money?",
        "body": "THE JOHNS HOPKINS UNIVERSITY APPLIED PHYSICS LABORATORY LLC is the top vendor with $132M in obligations. Other large vendors include C&T TECHNOLOGIES LLC at $38.6M and CITADEL FEDERAL SOLUTIONS LLC at $26.1M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences leads industry spending at $157M, and Other Computer Related Services follows at $134M. Engineering Services and Custom Computer Programming Services also appear among the top industries with $43.4M and $36.3M."
      }
    ]
  },
